# Environment & Tech Stack
- OS: Arch Linux (Wayland)
- Window Manager: Hyprland (Native Lua Configuration API)
- Theming Engine: Wallust (Dynamic color templates)
- Components: Waybar (CSS), SwayNC, Rofi, Kitty

# Coding & Formatting Standards
- Keep configurations strictly modular (use `dofile` imports in main entry points).
- Do not use deprecated syntax or variables from legacy Hyprland versions.
- For CSS styling (Waybar/SwayNC), rely strictly on Wallust template placeholders like `{{background}}`, `{{color4}}`, etc.
- Always output clean, complete configuration snippets without conversational filler.